    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive baserunning and favorable platoon splits. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) stands as our highest-ranked option, benefiting from a soft matchup against Lowder and a high-probability stolen base environment created by the opposing pitcher's slow delivery. We are also leaning heavily into **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.02); while **Yordan Alvarez** faces a slight platoon disadvantage, his elite xwOBA remains too impactful to fade, and **Christian Yelich** leverages a strong park factor and favorable platoon split to anchor the outfield. **Junior Caminero** (64.57) and **Lars Nootbaar** (62.90) remain solid secondary engines, with **Junior Caminero** getting a meaningful boost from his position in the three-hole, while **Lars Nootbaar** capitalizes on a high-upside matchup at the top of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the roster involves the utility spot and the exclusion of **Caleb Durbin** (45.43). While **Caleb Durbin** hovered near our marginal start threshold, he was ultimately benched because his efficiency metrics against Jax underperformed the higher-ceiling profiles of our confirmed starters. Meanwhile, we remain wary of the matchups for **Josh Smith** (43.18) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (42.03), both of whom are pushed to the brink of our bench floor due to facing an elite arm in deGrom. The low efficiency scores for **Josh Smith** and **Kazuma Okamoto** reflect the significant drag of deGrom\u2019s skill, and we are monitoring the lineup status of **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** closely; should either be absent from the official card, we may need to pivot to bench depth like **Carson Benge**, though he currently sits below our 40.0 baseline. We are holding **Colt Keith**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** in reserve as we monitor potential late-game pinch-hit opportunities.",
